; AlifePlus outpost service appearance pools, ONE SECTION PER FACTION. An outpost service spawns
; from the vanilla sim_default_<faction>_<role> profile, and most factions dress every role in the
; same model, so left alone a trader looks like any other stalker of his side and two outposts on a
; map look like the same man. The mutator dresses each service from its faction's pool here.
;
; FORMAT: one visual path per line, `N = <actor visual>`, read as an ORDERED list (the key is only
; an index; the value is the model). set_visual_name is applied verbatim. DLTX-overridable: override
; an index to swap a model, add an index to widen a pool, add a [ap_service_visual_<faction>] section
; to serve a new faction. A faction with no section or an empty one leaves its services in their
; spawn visual (logged at load).
;
; SELECTION: the mutator picks, for each new service, a model not already worn by another service of
; the SAME faction on the SAME level (one service per outpost, so per-smart is automatic), and stores
; the pick on the service so a reload keeps the same look. Order below is the tie-break start point.
;
; WHAT IS IN HERE, AND WHY ONLY THIS. Each entry's only wearers are generated sim_default profiles,
; so no named character shares a face with a service (probe-audited 2026-07-27: every model resolves
; to sim_default_* only). Every entry is referenced by a vanilla character_desc profile, so the mesh
; ships with the base game, not a modpack -- a missing model is Debug.fatal in CModelPool
; (ModelPool.cpp:110-124), never an invisible NPC. Exosuits excluded. Twelve per faction, ordered
; balaclavas and cloth masks first, then gasmasks and respirators, then helmets, then the visuals the
; faction's own generic service profiles wear, and a bare face only where a faction runs out. Nothing
; the base game ships reads as a shopkeeper -- every anonymous covered face it carries is combat gear
; -- so a mask is as close as the assets allow. Monolith owns 2 covered faces and ISG 4, so both
; fill from their own bare wardrobe; renegade has none of its own and wears bandit masks, four of
; which vanilla renegade profiles already use.

